- Oh, oh, and a helmet.

00:46:14.930 --> 00:46:17.290
- I go everywhere bicycle goes.

00:46:17.290 --> 00:46:18.650
I protect your head.

00:46:18.650 --> 00:46:20.730
You never get on a bike without me.

00:46:20.730 --> 00:46:23.020
- Oh, Elmo will remember that helmet.

00:46:23.020 --> 00:46:23.860
Thanks, helmet.

00:46:23.860 --> 00:46:25.740
Oh, now it's your turn, bicycle.

00:46:25.740 --> 00:46:27.660
- Oh, funny you should mention turn.

00:46:27.660 --> 00:46:30.000
See, you can turn me with my handlebar.

00:46:30.000 --> 00:46:47.770
You want to hear the story of Pecos Bill too?

00:46:47.770 --> 00:46:57.890
Pecos Bill was a rootin' tootin' cowboy, fear of a critter, big or small, he was the

00:46:57.890 --> 00:47:00.000
bravest and the best.

00:47:00.000 --> 00:47:05.380
The wild and wild wild west was the ridinest, ropinest, cowboy of them all.

00:47:05.380 --> 00:47:06.950
Oh, yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:47:06.950 --> 00:47:09.500
Now, yodelay, yodelay, yodelay.

00:47:09.500 --> 00:47:16.960
This ropinest cowboy of them all.

00:47:16.960 --> 00:47:17.570
Ah!
